#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:1
msgid "ADR-0012: Astronomical catalogues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P9.1 to P9.9 (REQ-CAT-1 to REQ-CAT-7, NF-7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:9
msgid ""
"LUMOS reads a dozen services (SIMBAD, VizieR, Gaia, CALSPEC, ESO, IRSA, "
"MAST, the NASA Exoplanet Archive, exoplanet.eu, JPL Horizons, the SVO "
"Filter Profile Service, SkyView, hips2fits) and must stay safe (TLS "
"always verified, timeouts), usable offline, testable without network, and"
" traceable (provenance of every value)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:13
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:15
msgid ""
"**One network layer** (`lumos.catalogs.http.fetch`): `https` only, TLS "
"verification that cannot be turned off, a timeout on every request, a "
"JSON user cache keyed by method, URL, parameters and body (7-day "
"lifetime), an offline mode, and an injectable transport (`requests` by "
"default). `LUMOS_CATALOGS_CACHE` and `LUMOS_CATALOGS_OFFLINE` set the "
"cache and the offline mode for notebooks and CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:19
msgid ""
"**Thin providers on standard protocols**: IVOA TAP (ADQL, VOTable read "
"with astropy) for SIMBAD, Gaia DR3, the NASA Exoplanet Archive "
"(`pscomppars`), IRSA (2MASS), ESO and MAST (ObsCore); plain HTTP for the "
"VizieR SED service, CALSPEC and Pickles files (STScI), the SVO FPS, JPL "
"Horizons (JSON API), SkyView and hips2fits. `astroquery` and `pyvo` are "
"not needed: the `[catalogs]` extra only holds `requests`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:23
msgid ""
"**exoplanet.eu** is read from its CSV catalogue (its TAP server refused "
"connections on 2026-10-16); the file (3.7 MB) is cached like any answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:25
msgid ""
"**Solar reference spectrum**: CALSPEC `sun_reference_stis` (Bohlin et al."
" 2001) instead of the ASTM E490 table, which is distributed as a "
"spreadsheet; both agree within a few percent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:27
msgid ""
"**Typed records** (`StarRecord`, `ExoplanetRecord`, `SolarSystemRecord`, "
"`ExtendedObjectRecord`): every field is a `Measurement` (value with unit,"
" uncertainty, provider, reference, `estimated` flag)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:29
msgid ""
"**SED fusion rules**: one point per filter, priority catalogues first "
"(`DEFAULT_PRIORITIES`), then the smallest relative uncertainty, then the "
"median; completion by a blackbody fit, flagged as estimated; a measured "
"effective temperature is kept and only the solid angle is fitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:32
msgid ""
"**Tests on recorded answers**: `tools/record_catalog_fixtures.py` records"
" the real answers with `requests` (independently of LUMOS) in "
"`tests/fixtures/catalogs`; a replay transport answers the requests of "
"LUMOS and refuses any other. Expected values are those of the catalogues,"
" cited in the tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:36
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:38
msgid ""
"`astroquery` everywhere: convenient, but heavy, with its own caches and "
"network settings that would bypass the guarantees of the network layer "
"(TLS, timeouts, offline mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:40
msgid ""
"Mocking parsed results instead of recording raw answers: the tests would "
"not check the parsing of the real formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:43
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:45
msgid ""
"Service changes (columns, formats) are caught by re-recording the "
"fixtures; network tests can be added under the `network` marker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0012-catalogues.md:47
msgid ""
"The cache of `examples/catalog_cache` must be re-recorded when the "
"notebook `06` changes its queries."
msgstr ""

